ICYEXT(1)                   Terminal ICY Tag Extractor                  ICYEXT(1)

NAME
       icyext - terminal ICY metadata extractor

SYNOPSIS
       icyext [-t] [-u url] url

DESCRIPTION
       icyext is a Perl script that accepts an internet radio URL either as an
       option or from standard input. If ICY metadata is available, it will be
       printed to standard error. By default, the audio stream is buffered and
       written unchanged to standard output. The program does not include any
       built‑in audio playback functionality.

       AAC streams can optionally be transcoded to MP3; see the -t option
       below.

       icyext was developed on NetBSD as part of a UPnP and internet radio
       project.

       Only Perl core modules are used. ffprobe and ffmpeg are required.

OPTIONS
       -h     Show a short usage message.

       -u URL
              Specify a URL. The URL may be an http(s) address or “-”.
              If “-” is used, the URL is read from standard input or a pipe.

              The same behavior applies when icyext - is used.

       -t     By default, the audio stream is passed through unchanged so the
              user may choose any external player. When -t is specified, AAC
              streams are transcoded to MP3. The transcoder attempts to use the
              next higher bitrate; for example, a 96k AAC stream will be
              transcoded to approximately 128k MP3. The maximum bitrate is
              capped at 320k.

              MP3 streams are never transcoded.

EXAMPLES
       Send a URL to icyext and play the stream with mpg123:

           echo "http://somemusic.com/stream.aac" | icyext -t - | mpg123 -q -

       Send a UPnP URL into the playback chain:

           upnpls .1.3.1.1@f=url | icyext -t - | mpg123 -q -

BUGS
       Probably.

